            "createdOn": 1772104489,
            "author": {
                "name": "Rex Fu",
                "email": "Rex.Fu@amd.com",
                "username": "tifu_amdeng"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 15,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Why are we doing this?  We should not be logging custom events for every GPIO."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 15,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Rex Fu",
                        "email": "Rex.Fu@amd.com",
                        "username": "tifu_amdeng"
                    },
                    "message": "Hi Patrick,\n\nThanks for the comment.\n\nThe intent of this change was not to introduce generic logging for all GPIO transitions. It was meant to cover a specific set of platform signals (presence, power status, and fault) that were previously untracked.\n\nThat said, I agree that logging raw GPIO transitions is not the right abstraction. I will narrow the scope so that only meaningful state changes are considered for logging, rather than treating all GPIO edges uniformly."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 15,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Rex Fu",
                        "email": "Rex.Fu@amd.com",
                        "username": "tifu_amdeng"
                    },
                    "message": "The implementation has been updated to use PowerRailFault/PowerRailFaultRecovered events instead of generic GPIO logging.\n\nEvents are generated only for power-domain signals and include recovery handling.\n\nPlease let me know if further adjustments are needed."
                }
            ],
